\s1 How Lonely Lies the City!
\r (\ref 2 Kings 24:10–17|2KI 24:10-17\ref*)
\q1 \v 1 \rb How|אֵיכָ֣ה׀\rb*\f + \fr 1:1 \ft This chapter is an acrostic poem, each verse beginning with the successive letters of the Hebrew alphabet.\f* \rb lonely|בָדָ֗ד\rb* \rb lies|יָשְׁבָ֣ה\rb* \rb the city|הָעִיר֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb once so full|רַבָּ֣תִי\rb* \rb of people|עָ֔ם\rb*!
\q1 \rb She who was great|רַּבָּ֣תִי\rb* \rb among the nations|בַגּוֹיִ֗ם\rb*
\q2 \rb has become|הָיְתָ֖ה\rb* \rb a widow|כְּאַלְמָנָ֑ה\rb*.
