\q2 \rb there is no one|אֵֽין־\rb* \rb to comfort her|מְנַחֵ֖ם\rb*.
\q1 \rb All|כָּל־\rb* \rb her friends|רֵעֶ֙יהָ֙\rb* \rb have betrayed|בָּ֣גְדוּ\rb* \rb her|בָ֔הּ\rb*;
\q2 \rb they have become|הָ֥יוּ\rb* \rb her|לָ֖הּ\rb* \rb enemies|לְאֹיְבִֽים׃ס\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 3 \rb Judah|יְהוּדָ֤ה\rb* \rb has gone into exile|גָּֽלְתָ֨ה\rb*
