\q2 \rb in the midst|בֵּ֥ין\rb* \rb of her distress|הַמְּצָרִֽים׃ס\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 4 \rb The roads|דַּרְכֵ֨י\rb* \rb to Zion|צִיּ֜וֹן\rb* \rb mourn|אֲבֵל֗וֹת\rb*,
\q2 \rb because no one|מִבְּלִי֙\rb* \rb comes|בָּאֵ֣י\rb* \rb to her appointed feasts|מוֹעֵ֔ד\rb*.
\q1 \rb All|כָּל־\rb* \rb her gates|שְׁעָרֶ֙יהָ֙\rb* \rb are deserted|שֽׁוֹמֵמִ֔ין\rb*;
\q2 \rb her priests|כֹּהֲנֶ֖יהָ\rb* \rb groan|נֶאֱנָחִ֑ים\rb*,
\q1 \rb her maidens|בְּתוּלֹתֶ֥יהָ\rb* \rb grieve|נּוּג֖וֹת\rb*,
\q2 \rb and she herself|וְהִ֥יא\rb* \rb is bitter with anguish|מַר־\rb*.
\b 
