\q1 \rb May You bring|הֵבֵ֥אתָ\rb* \rb the day|יוֹם־\rb* \rb You have announced|קָרָ֖אתָ\rb*,
\q2 \rb so that they may become|וְיִֽהְי֥וּ\rb* \rb like me|כָמֽוֹנִי׃ס\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 22 \rb Let all|כָל־\rb* \rb their wickedness|רָעָתָ֤ם\rb* \rb come|תָּבֹ֨א\rb* \rb before You|לְפָנֶ֙יךָ֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb and deal|וְעוֹלֵ֣ל\rb* \rb with them|לָ֔מוֹ\rb*
\q1 \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb You have dealt|עוֹלַ֛לְתָּ\rb* \rb with me|לִ֖י\rb*
\q2 \rb because of|עַ֣ל\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb my transgressions|פְּשָׁעָ֑י\rb*.
\q1 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb my groans|אַנְחֹתַ֖י\rb* \rb are many|רַבּ֥וֹת\rb*,
\q2 \rb and my heart|וְלִבִּ֥י\rb* \rb is faint|דַוָּֽי׃פ\rb*.
\c 2
\s1 God’s Anger over Jerusalem
\q1 \v 1 \rb How|אֵיכָה֩\rb*\f + \fr 2:1 \ft This chapter is an acrostic poem, each verse beginning with the successive letters of the Hebrew alphabet.\f* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb has covered|יָעִ֨יב\rb* \rb the Daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of Zion|צִיּ֔וֹן\rb*
\q2 \rb with the cloud of His anger|בְּאַפּ֤וֹ׀\rb*!
\q1 \rb He has cast|הִשְׁלִ֤יךְ\rb* \rb the glory|תִּפְאֶ֖רֶת\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*
\q2 \rb from heaven|מִשָּׁמַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb to earth|אֶ֔רֶץ\rb*.
\q1 \rb He has abandoned|וְלֹא־\rb*\rb |זָכַ֥ר\rb* \rb His footstool|הֲדֹם־\rb*\rb |רַגְלָ֖יו\rb*
\q2 \rb in the day|בְּי֥וֹם\rb* \rb of His anger|אַפּֽוֹ׃ס\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 2 \rb Without|לֹא\rb* \rb pity|חָמַ֗ל\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֜י\rb* \rb has swallowed up|בִּלַּ֨ע\rb*
\q2 \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the dwellings|נְא֣וֹת\rb* \rb of Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֔ב\rb*.
\q1 \rb In His wrath|בְּעֶבְרָת֛וֹ\rb* \rb He has demolished|הָרַ֧ס\rb*
\q2 \rb the fortified cities|מִבְצְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the Daughter|בַת־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb*.
\q1 \rb He brought|הִגִּ֣יעַ\rb* \rb to the ground|לָאָ֑רֶץ\rb* \rb and defiled|חִלֵּ֥ל\rb*
\q2 \rb her kingdom|מַמְלָכָ֖ה\rb* \rb and its princes|וְשָׂרֶֽיהָ׃ס\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 3 \rb In fierce|בָּֽחֳרִי\rb* \rb anger|אַ֗ף\rb* \rb He has cut off|גָּדַ֣ע\rb*
\q2 \rb every|כֹּ֚ל\rb* \rb horn|קֶ֣רֶן\rb*\f + \fr 2:3 \ft Or \fqa all the strength\f* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*
\q1 \rb and withdrawn|הֵשִׁ֥יב\rb*\rb |אָח֛וֹר\rb* \rb His right hand|יְמִינ֖וֹ\rb*
\q2 \rb at the approach|מִפְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the enemy|אוֹיֵ֑ב\rb*.
\q1 \rb He has burned|וַיִּבְעַ֤ר\rb* \rb in Jacob|בְּיַעֲקֹב֙\rb* \rb like a flaming|לֶֽהָבָ֔ה\rb* \rb fire|כְּאֵ֣שׁ\rb*
\q2 \rb that consumes|אָכְלָ֖ה\rb* \rb everything around it|סָבִֽיב׃ס\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 4 \rb He has bent|דָּרַ֨ךְ\rb* \rb His bow|קַשְׁתּ֜וֹ\rb* \rb like an enemy|כְּאוֹיֵ֗ב\rb*;
\q2 \rb His right hand|יְמִינוֹ֙\rb* \rb is positioned|נִצָּ֤ב\rb*.
\q1 \rb Like a foe|כְּצָ֔ר\rb* \rb He has killed|וַֽיַּהֲרֹ֔ג\rb*
\q2 \rb all|כֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb who were pleasing|מַחֲמַדֵּי־\rb* \rb to the eye|עָ֑יִן\rb*;
\q1 \rb He has poured out|שָׁפַ֥ךְ\rb* \rb His wrath|חֲמָתֽוֹ׃ס\rb* \rb like fire|כָּאֵ֖שׁ\rb*
\q2 \rb on the tent|בְּאֹ֙הֶל֙\rb* \rb of the Daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of Zion|צִיּ֔וֹן\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 5 \rb The Lord|אֲדֹנָ֤י׀\rb* \rb is|הָיָ֨ה\rb* \rb like an enemy|כְּאוֹיֵב֙\rb*;
\q2 \rb He has swallowed up|בִּלַּ֣ע\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*.
\q1 \rb He has swallowed up|בִּלַּע֙\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb her palaces|אַרְמְנוֹתֶ֔יהָ\rb*
\q2 \rb and destroyed|שִׁחֵ֖ת\rb* \rb her strongholds|מִבְצָרָ֑יו\rb*.
\q1 \rb He has multiplied|וַיֶּ֙רֶב֙\rb* \rb mourning|תַּאֲנִיָּ֖ה\rb* \rb and lamentation|וַאֲנִיָּֽה׃ס\rb*
\q2 \rb for the Daughter|בְּבַת־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 6 \rb He has laid waste|וַיַּחְמֹ֤ס\rb* \rb His tabernacle|שֻׂכּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb like a garden booth|כַּגַּן֙\rb*;
\q2 \rb He has destroyed|שִׁחֵ֖ת\rb* \rb His place of meeting|מוֹעֲד֑וֹ\rb*.
\q1 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֤ה׀\rb* \rb has made Zion forget|שִׁכַּ֨ח\rb*\rb |בְּצִיּוֹן֙\rb*
\q2 \rb her appointed feasts|מוֹעֵ֣ד\rb* \rb and Sabbaths|וְשַׁבָּ֔ת\rb*.
\q1 \rb In His fierce anger|בְּזַֽעַם־\rb*\rb |אַפּ֖וֹ\rb*
\q2 \rb He has despised|וַיִּנְאַ֥ץ\rb* \rb both king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb and priest|וְכֹהֵֽן׃ס\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 7 \rb The Lord|אֲדֹנָ֤י׀\rb* \rb has rejected|זָנַ֨ח\rb* \rb His altar|מִזְבְּחוֹ֙\rb*;
\q2 \rb He has abandoned|נִאֵ֣ר\rb* \rb His sanctuary|מִקְדָּשׁ֔וֹ\rb*;
\q1 \rb He has delivered|הִסְגִּיר֙\rb* \rb the walls|חוֹמֹ֖ת\rb* \rb of her palaces|אַרְמְנוֹתֶ֑יהָ\rb*
\q2 \rb into the hand|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb of the enemy|אוֹיֵ֔ב\rb*.
\q1 \rb They have raised|נָתְנ֥וּ\rb* \rb a shout|ק֛וֹל\rb* \rb in the house|בְּבֵית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*
\q2 \rb as on the day|כְּי֥וֹם\rb* \rb of an appointed feast|מוֹעֵֽד׃ס\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 8 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֤ה׀\rb* \rb determined|חָשַׁ֨ב\rb* \rb to destroy|לְהַשְׁחִית֙\rb*
\q2 \rb the wall|חוֹמַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the Daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of Zion|צִיּ֔וֹן\rb*.
\q1 \rb He stretched out|נָ֣טָה\rb* \rb a measuring line|קָ֔ו\rb*
\q2 \rb and did not|לֹא־\rb* \rb withdraw|הֵשִׁ֥יב\rb* \rb His hand|יָד֖וֹ\rb* \rb from destroying|מִבַּלֵּ֑עַ\rb*.
\q1 \rb He made the ramparts|חֵ֥ל\rb* \rb and walls|וְחוֹמָ֖ה\rb* \rb lament|וַיַּֽאֲבֶל־\rb*;
\q2 \rb together|יַחְדָּ֥ו\rb* \rb they waste away|אֻמְלָֽלוּ׃ס\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 9 \rb Her gates|שְׁעָרֶ֔יהָ\rb* \rb have sunk|טָבְע֤וּ\rb* \rb into the ground|בָאָ֙רֶץ֙\rb*;
\q2 \rb He has destroyed|אִבַּ֥ד\rb* \rb and shattered|וְשִׁבַּ֖ר\rb* \rb their bars|בְּרִיחֶ֑יהָ\rb*.
\q1 \rb Her king|מַלְכָּ֨הּ\rb* \rb and her princes|וְשָׂרֶ֤יהָ\rb* \rb are exiled among the nations|בַגּוֹיִם֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb the law|תּוֹרָ֔ה\rb* \rb is no more|אֵ֣ין\rb*,
\q1 \rb and even|גַּם־\rb* \rb her prophets|נְבִיאֶ֕יהָ\rb*
\q2 \rb find|מָצְא֥וּ\rb* \rb no|לֹא־\rb* \rb vision|חָז֖וֹן\rb* \rb from the LORD|מֵיְהוָֽה׃ס\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 10 \rb The elders|זִקְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the Daughter|בַת־\rb* \rb of Zion|צִיּ֔וֹן\rb*
\q2 \rb sit|יֵשְׁב֨וּ\rb* \rb on the ground|לָאָ֤רֶץ\rb* \rb in silence|יִדְּמוּ֙\rb*.
\q1 \rb They have thrown|הֶֽעֱל֤וּ\rb* \rb dust|עָפָר֙\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb their heads|רֹאשָׁ֔ם\rb*
\q2 \rb and put on|חָגְר֖וּ\rb* \rb sackcloth|שַׂקִּ֑ים\rb*.
\q1 \rb The young women|בְּתוּלֹ֖ת\rb* \rb of Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִָֽם׃ס\rb*
\q2 \rb have bowed|הוֹרִ֤ידוּ\rb* \rb their heads|רֹאשָׁ֔ן\rb* \rb to the ground|לָאָ֙רֶץ֙\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 11 \rb My eyes|עֵינַי֙\rb* \rb fail|כָּל֨וּ\rb* \rb from weeping|בַדְּמָע֤וֹת\rb*;
\q2 \rb I am churning|חֳמַרְמְר֣וּ\rb* \rb within|מֵעַ֔י\rb*.
\q1 \rb My heart|כְּבֵדִ֔י\rb* \rb is poured out|נִשְׁפַּ֤ךְ\rb* \rb in grief|לָאָ֙רֶץ֙\rb*
\q2 \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb the destruction|שֶׁ֖בֶר\rb* \rb of the daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of my people|עַמִּ֑י\rb*,
\q1 \rb because children|עוֹלֵל֙\rb* \rb and infants|וְיוֹנֵ֔ק\rb* \rb faint|בֵּֽעָטֵ֤ף\rb*
\q2 \rb in the streets|בִּרְחֹב֖וֹת\rb* \rb of the city|קִרְיָֽה׃ס\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 12 \rb They cry out|יֹֽאמְר֔וּ\rb* \rb to their mothers|לְאִמֹּתָם֙\rb*:
\q2 “\rb Where|אַיֵּ֖ה\rb* \rb is the grain|דָּגָ֣ן\rb* \rb and wine|וָיָ֑יִן\rb*?”
\q1 \rb as they faint|בְּהִֽתְעַטְּפָ֤ם\rb* \rb like the wounded|כֶּֽחָלָל֙\rb*
\q2 \rb in the streets|בִּרְחֹב֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the city|עִ֔יר\rb*,
\q1 \rb as their lives|נַפְשָׁ֔ם\rb* \rb fade away|בְּהִשְׁתַּפֵּ֣ךְ\rb*
\q2 \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb the arms|חֵ֖יק\rb* \rb of their mothers|אִמֹּתָֽם׃ס\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 13 \rb What|מָֽה־\rb* \rb can I say for you|אֲעִידֵ֞ךְ\rb*?
\q2 \rb To|לָּ֗ךְ\rb* \rb what|מָ֣ה\rb* \rb can I compare you|אֲדַמֶּה־\rb*,
\q2 \rb O Daughter|הַבַּת֙\rb* \rb of Jerusalem|יְר֣וּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb*?
\q1 \rb To|לָּךְ֙\rb* \rb what|מָ֤ה\rb* \rb can I liken you|אַשְׁוֶה־\rb*,
