\q2 \rb O Virgin|בְּתוּלַ֖ת\rb* \rb Daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of Zion|צִיּ֑וֹן\rb*?
\q1 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb your wound|שִׁבְרֵ֖ךְ\rb* \rb is as deep|גָד֥וֹל\rb* \rb as the sea|כַּיָּ֛ם\rb*.
\q2 \rb Who|מִ֥י\rb* \rb can ever heal|יִרְפָּא־\rb* \rb you|לָֽךְ׃ס\rb*?
\b 
\q1 \v 14 \rb The visions|חָ֤זוּ\rb* \rb of your prophets|נְבִיאַ֗יִךְ\rb*
\q2 \rb were empty|שָׁ֣וְא\rb* \rb and deceptive|וְתָפֵ֔ל\rb*;
\q1 \rb they did not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb expose|גִלּ֥וּ\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb your guilt|עֲוֺנֵ֖ךְ\rb*
\q2 \rb to ward off|לְהָשִׁ֣יב\rb* \rb your captivity|שְׁבִיתֵךְ\rb*.
\q1 \rb The burdens|מַשְׂא֥וֹת\rb* \rb they envisioned|וַיֶּ֣חֱזוּ\rb* \rb for you|לָ֔ךְ\rb*
\q2 \rb were empty|שָׁ֖וְא\rb* \rb and misleading|וּמַדּוּחִֽים׃ס\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 15 \rb All|כָּל־\rb* \rb who pass by|עֹ֣בְרֵי\rb*\rb |דֶ֔רֶךְ\rb*
\q2 \rb clap|סָֽפְק֨וּ\rb* \rb their hands|כַּפַּ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb at you in scorn|עָלַ֤יִךְ\rb*.
\q1 \rb They hiss|שָֽׁרְקוּ֙\rb* \rb and shake|וַיָּנִ֣עוּ\rb* \rb their heads|רֹאשָׁ֔ם\rb*
\q2 \rb at|עַל־\rb* \rb the Daughter|בַּ֖ת\rb* \rb of Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb*:
