\q2 \rb the perfection|כְּלִ֣ילַת\rb* \rb of beauty|יֹ֔פִי\rb*,
\q2 \rb the joy|מָשׂ֖וֹשׂ\rb* \rb of all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָֽרֶץ׃ס\rb*?”
\b 
\q1 \v 16 \rb All|כָּל־\rb* \rb your enemies|א֣וֹיְבַ֔יִךְ\rb*
\q2 \rb open|פָּצ֨וּ\rb* \rb their mouths|פִּיהֶם֙\rb* \rb against you|עָלַ֤יִךְ\rb*.
\q1 \rb They hiss|שָֽׁרְקוּ֙\rb* \rb and gnash|וַיַּֽחַרְקוּ־\rb* \rb their teeth|שֵׁ֔ן\rb*,
\q2 \rb saying|אָמְר֖וּ\rb*, “\rb We have swallowed her up|בִּלָּ֑עְנוּ\rb*.\rb |אַ֣ךְ\rb*
\q1 \rb This|זֶ֥ה\rb* \rb is the day|הַיּ֛וֹם\rb* \rb for which we have waited|שֶׁקִּוִּינֻ֖הוּ\rb*.
\q2 \rb We have lived|מָצָ֥אנוּ\rb* \rb to see it|רָאִֽינוּ׃ס\rb*!”
\b 
\q1 \v 17 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb has done|עָשָׂ֨ה\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb He planned|זָמָ֗ם\rb*;
\q2 \rb He has accomplished|בִּצַּ֤ע\rb* \rb His decree|אֶמְרָתוֹ֙\rb*,
\q1 \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb He ordained|צִוָּ֣ה\rb* \rb in days|מִֽימֵי־\rb* \rb of old|קֶ֔דֶם\rb*;
\q2 \rb He has overthrown you|הָרַ֖ס\rb* \rb without|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb pity|חָמָ֑ל\rb*.
\q1 \rb He has let the enemy|אוֹיֵ֔ב\rb* \rb gloat|וַיְשַׂמַּ֤ח\rb* \rb over you|עָלַ֙יִךְ֙\rb*
\q2 \rb and exalted|הֵרִ֖ים\rb* \rb the horn|קֶ֥רֶן\rb*\f + \fr 2:17 \ft Or \fqa the strength\f* \rb of your foes|צָרָֽיִךְ׃ס\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 18 \rb The hearts of the people|לִבָּ֖ם\rb*
\q2 \rb cry out|צָעַ֥ק\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֑י\rb*.\f + \fr 2:18 \ft Literally \fqa Their heart cries out to the Lord.\f*
\q1 \rb O wall|חוֹמַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the Daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of Zion|צִ֠יּוֹן\rb*,
\q2 \rb let your tears|דִּמְעָה֙\rb* \rb run down|הוֹרִ֨ידִי\rb* \rb like a river|כַנַּ֤חַל\rb*
\q2 \rb day|יוֹמָ֣ם\rb* \rb and night|וָלַ֔יְלָה\rb*.
\q1 \rb Give|תִּתְּנִ֤י\rb* \rb yourself|לָ֔ךְ\rb* \rb no|אַֽל־\rb* \rb relief|פוּגַת֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb and your eyes|עֵינֵֽךְ׃ס\rb*\rb |בַּת־\rb* \rb no|אַל־\rb* \rb rest|תִּדֹּ֖ם\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 19 \rb Arise|ק֣וּמִי׀\rb*, \rb cry out|רֹ֣נִּי\rb* \rb in the night|בַלַּיִל\rb*
\q2 \rb from the first|לְרֹאשׁ֙\rb* \rb watch of the night|אַשְׁמֻר֔וֹת\rb*.\f + \fr 2:19 \ft That is, between six and nine at night\f*
\q1 \rb Pour out|שִׁפְכִ֤י\rb* \rb your heart|לִבֵּ֔ךְ\rb* \rb like water|כַמַּ֙יִם֙\rb*
\q2 \rb in|נֹ֖כַח\rb* \rb the presence|פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֑י\rb*.
\q1 \rb Lift up|שְׂאִ֧י\rb* \rb your hands|כַּפַּ֗יִךְ\rb* \rb to Him|אֵלָ֣יו\rb*
\q2 \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb the lives|נֶ֙פֶשׁ֙\rb* \rb of your children|עֽוֹלָלַ֔יִךְ\rb*
\q1 \rb who are fainting|הָעֲטוּפִ֥ים\rb* \rb from hunger|בְּרָעָ֖ב\rb*
\q2 \rb on the corner|בְּרֹ֥אשׁ\rb* \rb of every|כָּל־\rb* \rb street|חוּצֽוֹת׃ס\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 20 \rb Look|רְאֵ֤ה\rb*, \rb O LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*, \rb and consider|וְֽהַבִּ֔יטָה\rb*:
\q2 \rb Whom|לְמִ֖י\rb* \rb have You ever treated|עוֹלַ֣לְתָּ\rb* \rb like this|כֹּ֑ה\rb*?
\q1 \rb Should|אִם־\rb* \rb women|נָשִׁ֤ים\rb* \rb eat|תֹּאכַ֨לְנָה\rb* \rb their offspring|פִּרְיָם֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb the infants|עֹלֲלֵ֣י\rb* \rb they have nurtured|טִפֻּחִ֔ים\rb*?
\q1 \rb Should priests|כֹּהֵ֥ן\rb* \rb and prophets|וְנָבִֽיא׃ס\rb* \rb be killed|יֵהָרֵ֛ג\rb*
\q2 \rb in the sanctuary|בְּמִקְדַּ֥שׁ\rb* \rb of the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֖י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb*?
\b 
\q1 \v 21 \rb Both young|נַ֣עַר\rb* \rb and old|וְזָקֵ֔ן\rb* \rb lie together|שָׁכְב֨וּ\rb*
\q2 \rb in the dust|לָאָ֤רֶץ\rb* \rb of the streets|חוּצוֹת֙\rb*.
\q1 \rb My young men|וּבַחוּרַ֖י\rb* \rb and maidens|בְּתוּלֹתַ֥י\rb*
\q2 \rb have fallen|נָפְל֣וּ\rb* \rb by the sword|בֶחָ֑רֶב\rb*.
\q1 \rb You have slain them|הָרַ֙גְתָּ֙\rb* \rb in the day|בְּי֣וֹם\rb* \rb of Your anger|אַפֶּ֔ךָ\rb*;
\q2 \rb You have slaughtered them|טָבַ֖חְתָּ\rb* \rb without|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb compassion|חָמָֽלְתָּ׃ס\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 22 \rb You summoned|תִּקְרָא֩\rb* \rb my terrors|מְגוּרַי֙\rb* \rb on every side|מִסָּבִ֔יב\rb*,
\q2 \rb as for the day|כְי֨וֹם\rb* \rb of an appointed feast|מוֹעֵ֤ד\rb*.
\q1 \rb In the day|בְּי֥וֹם\rb* \rb of the LORD’s|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb anger|אַף־\rb*
