\q1 \rb my enemy|אֹיְבִ֥י\rb* \rb has destroyed|כִלָּֽם׃פ\rb*
\q2 \rb those|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I nurtured|טִפַּ֥חְתִּי\rb* \rb and reared|וְרִבִּ֖יתִי\rb*.
\c 3
\s1 The Prophet’s Afflictions
\q1 \v 1 \rb I|אֲנִ֤י\rb*\f + \fr 3:1 \ft This chapter is an acrostic poem, each 3–verse stanza beginning with the successive letters of the Hebrew alphabet.\f* \rb am the man|הַגֶּ֙בֶר֙\rb* \rb who has seen|רָאָ֣ה\rb* \rb affliction|עֳנִ֔י\rb*
\q2 \rb under the rod|בְּשֵׁ֖בֶט\rb* \rb of God’s wrath|עֶבְרָתֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 2 \rb |אוֹתִ֥י\rb* \rb He has driven me away|נָהַ֛ג\rb* \rb and made me walk|וַיֹּלַ֖ךְ\rb*
\q2 \rb in darkness|חֹ֥שֶׁךְ\rb* \rb instead of|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb light|אֽוֹר׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 3 \rb Indeed|אַ֣ךְ\rb*, \rb He keeps turning|יָשֻׁ֛ב\rb*\rb |יַהֲפֹ֥ךְ\rb* \rb His hand|יָד֖וֹ\rb*
\q2 \rb against me|בִּ֥י\rb* \rb all day long|כָּל־\rb*\rb |הַיּֽוֹם׃ס\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 4 \rb He has worn away|בִּלָּ֤ה\rb* \rb my flesh|בְשָׂרִי֙\rb* \rb and skin|וְעוֹרִ֔י\rb*;
\q2 \rb He has shattered|שִׁבַּ֖ר\rb* \rb my bones|עַצְמוֹתָֽי׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 5 \rb He has besieged|בָּנָ֥ה\rb* \rb me|עָלַ֛י\rb* \rb and surrounded me|וַיַּקַּ֖ף\rb*
\q2 \rb with bitterness|רֹ֥אשׁ\rb* \rb and hardship|וּתְלָאָֽה׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 6 \rb He has made me dwell|הוֹשִׁיבַ֖נִי\rb* \rb in darkness|בְּמַחֲשַׁכִּ֥ים\rb*
\q2 \rb like those dead|כְּמֵתֵ֥י\rb* \rb for ages|עוֹלָֽם׃ס\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 7 \rb He has walled me in|גָּדַ֧ר\rb*\rb |בַּעֲדִ֛י\rb* \rb so I cannot|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb escape|אֵצֵ֖א\rb*;
\q2 \rb He has weighed me down|הִכְבִּ֥יד\rb* \rb with chains|נְחָשְׁתִּֽי׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 8 \rb Even|גַּ֣ם\rb* \rb when|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb I cry out|אֶזְעַק֙\rb* \rb and plead for help|וַאֲשַׁוֵּ֔עַ\rb*,
\q2 \rb He shuts out|שָׂתַ֖ם\rb* \rb my prayer|תְּפִלָּתִֽי׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 9 \rb He has barred|גָּדַ֤ר\rb* \rb my ways|דְּרָכַי֙\rb* \rb with cut stones|בְּגָזִ֔ית\rb*;
\q2 \rb He has made my paths|נְתִיבֹתַ֖י\rb* \rb crooked|עִוָּֽה׃ס\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 10 \rb He|הוּא֙\rb* \rb is a bear|דֹּ֣ב\rb* \rb lying in wait|אֹרֵ֥ב\rb*,
\q2 \rb a lion|אַרְיֵה\rb* \rb hiding in ambush|בְּמִסְתָּרִֽים׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 11 \rb He forced me off|סוֹרֵ֛ר\rb* \rb my path|דְּרָכַ֥י\rb* \rb and tore me to pieces|וַֽיְפַשְּׁחֵ֖נִי\rb*;
\q2 \rb He left me|שָׂמַ֥נִי\rb* \rb without help|שֹׁמֵֽם׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 12 \rb He bent|דָּרַ֤ךְ\rb* \rb His bow|קַשְׁתוֹ֙\rb*
\q2 \rb and set me|וַיַּצִּיבֵ֔נִי\rb* \rb as the target|כַּמַּטָּרָ֖א\rb* \rb for His arrow|לַחֵֽץ׃ס\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 13 \rb He pierced|הֵבִיא֙\rb* \rb my kidneys|בְּכִלְיוֹתָ֔י\rb*
\q2 \rb with His arrows|בְּנֵ֖י\rb*\rb |אַשְׁפָּתֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 14 \rb I am|הָיִ֤יתִי\rb* \rb a laughingstock|שְּׂחֹק֙\rb* \rb to all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb my people|עַמִּ֔י\rb*;
\q2 \rb they mock me in song|נְגִינָתָ֖ם\rb* \rb all day long|כָּל־\rb*\rb |הַיּֽוֹם׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 15 \rb He has filled me|הִשְׂבִּיעַ֥נִי\rb* \rb with bitterness|בַמְּרוֹרִ֖ים\rb*;
\q2 \rb He has intoxicated me|הִרְוַ֥נִי\rb* \rb with wormwood|לַעֲנָֽה׃ס\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 16 \rb He has ground|וַיַּגְרֵ֤ס\rb* \rb my teeth|שִׁנָּ֔י\rb* \rb with gravel|בֶּֽחָצָץ֙\rb*
\q2 \rb and trampled me|הִכְפִּישַׁ֖נִי\rb* \rb in the dust|בָּאֵֽפֶר׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 17 \rb My soul|נַפְשִׁ֖י\rb* \rb has been deprived|וַתִּזְנַ֧ח\rb* \rb of peace|מִשָּׁל֛וֹם\rb*;
\q2 \rb I have forgotten|נָשִׁ֥יתִי\rb* \rb what prosperity is|טוֹבָֽה׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 18 \rb So I say|וָאֹמַר֙\rb*, “\rb My strength|נִצְחִ֔י\rb* \rb has perished|אָבַ֣ד\rb*,
\q2 \rb along with my hope|וְתוֹחַלְתִּ֖י\rb* \rb from the LORD|מֵיְהוָֽה׃ס\rb*.”
\s1 The Prophet’s Hope
\q1 \v 19 \rb Remember|זְכָר־\rb* \rb my affliction|עָנְיִ֥י\rb* \rb and wandering|וּמְרוּדִ֖י\rb*,
\q2 \rb the wormwood|לַעֲנָ֥ה\rb* \rb and the gall|וָרֹֽאשׁ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 20 \rb Surely|זָכ֣וֹר\rb* \rb my soul|נַפְשִֽׁי׃\rb* \rb remembers|תִּזְכּ֔וֹר\rb*
\q2 \rb and is humbled|וְתָשִׁיחַ\rb* \rb within me|עָלַ֖י\rb*.
\q1 \v 21 \rb Yet I call|אָשִׁ֥יב\rb* \rb this|זֹ֛את\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb mind|לִבִּ֖י\rb*,
\q2 \rb and therefore|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb I have hope|אוֹחִֽיל׃ס\rb*:
\b 
\q1 \v 22 \rb Because of|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb the loving devotion|חַֽסְדֵ֤י\rb*\f + \fr 3:22 \ft Forms of the Hebrew \fqa chesed \ft are translated here and in most cases throughout the Scriptures as \fqa loving devotion\ft ; the range of meaning includes \fqa love\ft , \fqa goodness\ft , \fqa kindness\ft , \fqa faithfulness\ft , and \fqa mercy\ft , as well as \fqa loyalty to a covenant\ft .\f* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb we are not|לֹא־\rb* \rb consumed|תָ֔מְנוּ\rb*,
\q2 \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb His mercies|רַחֲמָֽיו׃\rb* \rb never|לֹא־\rb* \rb fail|כָל֖וּ\rb*.
\q1 \v 23 \rb They are new every morning|חֲדָשִׁים֙\rb*\rb |לַבְּקָרִ֔ים\rb*;
\q2 \rb great|רַבָּ֖ה\rb* \rb is Your faithfulness|אֱמוּנָתֶֽךָ׃\rb*!
\q1 \v 24 “\rb The LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb is my portion|חֶלְקִ֤י\rb*,” \rb says|אָמְרָ֣ה\rb* \rb my soul|נַפְשִׁ֔י\rb*,
\q2 “\rb therefore|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb I will hope|אוֹחִ֥יל\rb* \rb in Him|לֽוֹ׃ס\rb*.”
\b 
\q1 \v 25 \rb The LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb is good|ט֤וֹב\rb* \rb to those who wait for Him|לְקוָֹ֔ו\rb*,
\q2 \rb to the soul|לְנֶ֖פֶשׁ\rb* \rb who seeks Him|תִּדְרְשֶֽׁנּוּ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 26 \rb It is good|ט֤וֹב\rb* \rb to wait|וְיָחִיל֙\rb* \rb quietly|וְדוּמָ֔ם\rb*
\q2 \rb for the salvation|לִתְשׁוּעַ֖ת\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 27 \rb It is good|ט֣וֹב\rb* \rb for a man|לַגֶּ֔בֶר\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb to bear|יִשָּׂ֥א\rb* \rb the yoke|עֹ֖ל\rb*
\q2 \rb while he is still young|בִּנְעוּרָֽיו׃ס\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 28 \rb Let him sit|יֵשֵׁ֤ב\rb* \rb alone|בָּדָד֙\rb* \rb in silence|וְיִדֹּ֔ם\rb*,
\q2 \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD has laid it|נָטַ֖ל\rb* \rb upon him|עָלָֽיו׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 29 \rb Let him bury|יִתֵּ֤ן\rb* \rb his face|פִּ֔יהוּ\rb* \rb in the dust|בֶּֽעָפָר֙\rb*—
\q2 \rb perhaps|אוּלַ֖י\rb* \rb there is|יֵ֥שׁ\rb* \rb still hope|תִּקְוָֽה׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 30 \rb Let him offer|יִתֵּ֧ן\rb* \rb his cheek|לֶ֖חִי\rb* \rb to the one who would strike him|לְמַכֵּ֛הוּ\rb*;
\q2 \rb let him be filled|יִשְׂבַּ֥ע\rb* \rb with reproach|בְּחֶרְפָּֽה׃ס\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 31 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָֽי׃\rb* \rb will not|לֹ֥א\rb*
\q2 \rb cast us off|יִזְנַ֛ח\rb* \rb forever|לְעוֹלָ֖ם\rb*.
\q1 \v 32 \rb Even|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb He causes grief|הוֹגָ֔ה\rb*, \rb He will show compassion|וְרִחַ֖ם\rb*
\q2 \rb according to His abundant|כְּרֹ֥ב\rb* \rb loving devotion|חַסְדּוֹ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 33 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb He does not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb willingly|מִלִּבּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb afflict|עִנָּה֙\rb*
\q2 \rb or grieve|וַיַּגֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb the sons|בְנֵי־\rb* \rb of men|אִֽישׁ׃ס\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 34 \rb To crush|לְדַכֵּא֙\rb* \rb underfoot|תַּ֣חַת\rb*\rb |רַגְלָ֔יו\rb*
\q2 \rb all|כֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb the prisoners|אֲסִ֥ירֵי\rb* \rb of the land|אָֽרֶץ׃\rb*,
\q1 \v 35 \rb to deny|לְהַטּוֹת֙\rb* \rb a man|גָּ֔בֶר\rb* \rb justice|מִשְׁפַּט־\rb*
\q2 \rb before|נֶ֖גֶד\rb*\rb |פְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the Most High|עֶלְיֽוֹן׃\rb*,
\q1 \v 36 \rb to subvert|לְעַוֵּ֤ת\rb* \rb a man|אָדָם֙\rb* \rb in his lawsuit|בְּרִיב֔וֹ\rb*—
\q2 \rb of these the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֖י\rb* \rb does not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb approve|רָאָֽה׃ס\rb*.
\s1 God’s Justice
\q1 \v 37 \rb Who|מִ֣י\rb*\rb |זֶ֤ה\rb* \rb has spoken|אָמַר֙\rb* \rb and it came to pass|וַתֶּ֔הִי\rb*,
\q2 \rb unless|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֖י\rb* \rb has ordained it?|צִוָּֽה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 38 \rb Do not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb both adversity|הָרָע֖וֹת\rb* \rb and good|וְהַטּֽוֹב׃\rb*
\q2 \rb come|תֵצֵ֔א\rb* \rb from the mouth|מִפִּ֤י\rb* \rb of the Most High|עֶלְיוֹן֙\rb*?
\q1 \v 39 \rb Why|מַה־\rb* \rb should any mortal|חָ֔י\rb* \rb man|אָדָ֣ם\rb* \rb complain|יִּתְאוֹנֵן֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb in view of|עַל־\rb* \rb his|גֶּ֖בֶר\rb* \rb sins|חֶטְאוֹ׃ס\rb*?
\b 
\q1 \v 40 \rb Let us examine|נַחְפְּשָׂ֤ה\rb* \rb and test|וְֽנַחְקֹ֔רָה\rb* \rb our ways|דְרָכֵ֙ינוּ֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb and turn back|וְנָשׁ֖וּבָה\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 41 \rb Let us lift up|נִשָּׂ֤א\rb* \rb our hearts|לְבָבֵ֙נוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb and hands|כַּפָּ֔יִם\rb*
\q2 \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb God|אֵ֖ל\rb* \rb in heaven|בַּשָּׁמָֽיִם׃\rb*:
\q1 \v 42 “\rb We|נַ֤חְנוּ\rb* \rb have sinned|פָשַׁ֙עְנוּ֙\rb* \rb and rebelled|וּמָרִ֔ינוּ\rb*;
\q2 \rb You|אַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb have not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb forgiven|סָלָֽחְתָּ׃ס\rb*.”
\b 
\q1 \v 43 \rb You have covered|סַכֹּ֤תָה\rb* \rb Yourself in anger|בָאַף֙\rb* \rb and pursued us|וַֽתִּרְדְּפֵ֔נוּ\rb*;
\q2 \rb You have killed|הָרַ֖גְתָּ\rb* \rb without|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb pity|חָמָֽלְתָּ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 44 \rb You have covered|סַכּ֤וֹתָה\rb* \rb Yourself|לָ֔ךְ\rb* \rb with a cloud|בֶֽעָנָן֙\rb*
\q2 \rb that no prayer|תְּפִלָּֽה׃\rb* \rb can pass through|מֵעֲב֖וֹר\rb*.
\q1 \v 45 \rb You have made us|תְּשִׂימֵ֖נוּ\rb* \rb scum|סְחִ֧י\rb* \rb and refuse|וּמָא֛וֹס\rb*
\q2 \rb among|בְּקֶ֥רֶב\rb* \rb the nations|הָעַמִּֽים׃ס\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 46 \rb All|כָּל־\rb* \rb our enemies|אֹיְבֵֽינוּ׃\rb*
\q2 \rb open|פָּצ֥וּ\rb* \rb their mouths|פִּיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb against us|עָלֵ֛ינוּ\rb*.
