\q2 \rb than the eagles|מִנִּשְׁרֵ֖י\rb* \rb in the sky|שָׁמָ֑יִם\rb*;
\q1 \rb they pursued us|דְּלָקֻ֔נוּ\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb the mountains|הֶהָרִ֣ים\rb*
\q2 \rb and ambushed|אָ֥רְבוּ\rb* \rb us|לָֽנוּ׃ס\rb* \rb in the wilderness|בַּמִּדְבָּ֖ר\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 20 \rb The LORD’s|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb anointed|מְשִׁ֣יחַ\rb*, \rb the breath|ר֤וּחַ\rb* \rb of our life|אַפֵּ֙ינוּ֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb was captured|נִלְכַּ֖ד\rb* \rb in their pits|בִּשְׁחִיתוֹתָ֑ם\rb*.
\q1 \rb We had said|אָמַ֔רְנוּ\rb* \rb of him|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*,
\q2 “\rb Under his shadow|בְּצִלּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb we will live|נִֽחְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb among the nations|בַגּוֹיִֽם׃ס\rb*.”
\b 
\q1 \v 21 \rb So rejoice|שִׂ֤ישִׂי\rb* \rb and be glad|וְשִׂמְחִי֙\rb*, \rb O Daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of Edom|אֱד֔וֹם\rb*,
\q2 \rb you who dwell|יוֹשַׁבְתִּי\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Uz|ע֑וּץ\rb*.
\q1 \rb Yet the cup|כּ֔וֹס\rb* \rb will pass|תַּעֲבָר־\rb* \rb to|עָלַ֙יִךְ֙\rb* \rb you as well|גַּם־\rb*;
\q2 \rb you will get drunk|תִּשְׁכְּרִ֖י\rb* \rb and expose yourself|וְתִתְעָרִֽי׃ס\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 22 \rb O Daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of Zion|צִיּ֔וֹן\rb*, \rb your punishment|עֲוֺנֵךְ֙\rb* \rb is complete|תַּם־\rb*;
\q2 \rb He will not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb prolong|יוֹסִ֖יף\rb* \rb your exile|לְהַגְלוֹתֵ֑ךְ\rb*.\f + \fr 4:22 \ft Or \fqa He will not exile you again\f*
\q1 \rb But He will punish|פָּקַ֤ד\rb* \rb your iniquity|עֲוֺנֵךְ֙\rb*, \rb O Daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of Edom|אֱד֔וֹם\rb*;
\q2 \rb He will expose|גִּלָּ֖ה\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb your sins|חַטֹּאתָֽיִךְ׃פ\rb*.
\c 5
\s1 A Prayer for Restoration
\q1 \v 1 \rb Remember|זְכֹ֤ר\rb*, \rb O LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*, \rb what|מֶֽה־\rb* \rb has happened|הָ֣יָה\rb* \rb to us|לָ֔נוּ\rb*.
\q2 \rb Look|הַבֵּיט\rb* \rb and see|וּרְאֵ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb our disgrace|חֶרְפָּתֵֽנוּ׃\rb*!
\q1 \v 2 \rb Our inheritance|נַחֲלָתֵ֙נוּ֙\rb* \rb has been turned over|נֶֽהֶפְכָ֣ה\rb* \rb to strangers|לְזָרִ֔ים\rb*,
\q2 \rb our houses|בָּתֵּ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb to foreigners|לְנָכְרִֽים׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 3 \rb We have become|הָיִ֙ינוּ֙\rb* \rb fatherless|אֵין\rb*\rb |אָ֔ב\rb* \rb orphans|יְתוֹמִ֤ים\rb*;
\q2 \rb our mothers|אִמֹּתֵ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb are widows|כְּאַלְמָנֽוֹת׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 4 \rb We must buy|בְּכֶ֣סֶף\rb* \rb the water|מֵימֵ֙ינוּ֙\rb* \rb we drink|שָׁתִ֔ינוּ\rb*;
\q2 \rb our wood|עֵצֵ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb comes|יָבֹֽאוּ׃\rb* \rb at a price|בִּמְחִ֥יר\rb*.
\q1 \v 5 \rb We are closely|עַ֤ל\rb*\rb |צַוָּארֵ֙נוּ֙\rb* \rb pursued|נִרְדָּ֔פְנוּ\rb*;
\q2 \rb we are weary|יָגַ֖עְנוּ\rb* \rb and find no|לֹא\rb* \rb rest|הֽוּנַ֖ח\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 6 \rb We submitted|נָתַ֣נּוּ\rb*\rb |יָ֔ד\rb* \rb to Egypt|מִצְרַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb and Assyria|אַשּׁ֖וּר\rb*
\q2 \rb to get enough|לִשְׂבֹּ֥עַֽ\rb* \rb bread|לָֽחֶם׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 7 \rb Our fathers|אֲבֹתֵ֤ינוּ\rb* \rb sinned|חָֽטְאוּ֙\rb* \rb and are no more|אֵינָם\rb*,
\q2 \rb but we|אֲנַחְנוּ\rb* \rb bear|סָבָֽלְנוּ׃\rb* \rb their punishment|עֲוֺנֹתֵיהֶ֥ם\rb*.
\q1 \v 8 \rb Slaves|עֲבָדִים֙\rb* \rb rule|מָ֣שְׁלוּ\rb* \rb over us|בָ֔נוּ\rb*;
\q2 \rb there is no one|אֵ֥ין\rb* \rb to deliver us|פֹּרֵ֖ק\rb* \rb from their hands|מִיָּדָֽם׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 9 \rb We get|נָבִ֣יא\rb* \rb our bread|לַחְמֵ֔נוּ\rb* \rb at the risk of our lives|בְּנַפְשֵׁ֙נוּ֙\rb*
\q2 \rb because of|מִפְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb the sword|חֶ֥רֶב\rb* \rb in the wilderness|הַמִּדְבָּֽר׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 10 \rb Our skin|עוֹרֵ֙נוּ֙\rb* \rb is as hot|נִכְמָ֔רוּ\rb* \rb as an oven|כְּתַנּ֣וּר\rb*
\q2 \rb with|מִפְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb fever|זַלְעֲפ֥וֹת\rb* \rb from our hunger|רָעָֽב׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 11 \rb Women|נָשִׁים֙\rb* \rb have been ravished|עִנּ֔וּ\rb* \rb in Zion|בְּצִיּ֣וֹן\rb*,
\q2 \rb virgins|בְּתֻלֹ֖ת\rb* \rb in the cities|בְּעָרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 12 \rb Princes|שָׂרִים֙\rb* \rb have been hung up|נִתְל֔וּ\rb* \rb by their hands|בְּיָדָ֣ם\rb*;
\q2 \rb elders|זְקֵנִ֖ים\rb* \rb receive no|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb respect|פְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |נֶהְדָּֽרוּ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 13 \rb Young men|בַּחוּרִים֙\rb* \rb toil|נָשָׂ֔אוּ\rb* \rb at millstones|טְח֣וֹן\rb*;
\q2 \rb boys|וּנְעָרִ֖ים\rb* \rb stagger|כָּשָֽׁלוּ׃\rb* \rb under loads of wood|בָּעֵ֥ץ\rb*.
\q1 \v 14 \rb The elders|זְקֵנִים֙\rb* \rb have left|שָׁבָ֔תוּ\rb* \rb the city gate|מִשַּׁ֣עַר\rb*;
\q2 \rb the young men|בַּחוּרִ֖ים\rb* \rb have stopped their music|מִנְּגִינָתָֽם׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 15 \rb Joy|מְשׂ֣וֹשׂ\rb* \rb has left|שָׁבַת֙\rb* \rb our hearts|לִבֵּ֔נוּ\rb*;
\q2 \rb our dancing|מְחֹלֵֽנוּ׃\rb* \rb has turned|נֶהְפַּ֥ךְ\rb* \rb to mourning|לְאֵ֖בֶל\rb*.
\q1 \v 16 \rb The crown|עֲטֶ֣רֶת\rb* \rb has fallen|נָֽפְלָה֙\rb* \rb from our head|רֹאשֵׁ֔נוּ\rb*.
\q2 \rb Woe|אֽוֹי־\rb*\rb |נָ֥א\rb* \rb to us|לָ֖נוּ\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb we have sinned|חָטָֽאנוּ׃\rb*!
\b 
\q1 \v 17 \rb Because of|עַל־\rb* \rb this|זֶ֗ה\rb*, \rb our hearts|לִבֵּ֔נוּ\rb* \rb are|הָיָ֤ה\rb* \rb faint|דָוֶה֙\rb*;
\q2 \rb because of|עַל־\rb* \rb these|אֵ֖לֶּה\rb*, \rb our eyes|עֵינֵֽינוּ׃\rb* \rb grow dim|חָשְׁכ֥וּ\rb*—
\q1 \v 18 \rb because of|עַ֤ל\rb* \rb Mount|הַר־\rb* \rb Zion|צִיּוֹן֙\rb*, \rb which lies desolate|שֶׁשָּׁמֵ֔ם\rb*,
\q2 \rb patrolled|הִלְּכוּ־\rb* \rb by foxes|שׁוּעָלִ֖ים\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 19 \rb You|אַתָּ֤ה\rb*, \rb O LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*, \rb reign|תֵּשֵׁ֔ב\rb* \rb forever|לְעוֹלָ֣ם\rb*;
\q2 \rb Your throne|כִּסְאֲךָ֖\rb* \rb endures from generation|לְדֹ֥ר\rb* \rb to generation|וָדֽוֹר׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 20 \rb Why|לָ֤מָּה\rb* \rb have You forgotten us|תִּשְׁכָּחֵ֔נוּ\rb* \rb forever|לָנֶ֙צַח֙\rb*?
\q2 \rb Why have You forsaken us|תַּֽעַזְבֵ֖נוּ\rb* \rb for so long|לְאֹ֥רֶךְ\rb*\rb |יָמִֽים׃\rb*?
\q1 \v 21 \rb Restore us|הֲשִׁיבֵ֨נוּ\rb* \rb to Yourself|אֵלֶ֙יךָ֙\rb*, \rb O LORD|יְהוָ֤ה׀\rb*, \rb so we may return|וְנָשׁוּב\rb*;
\q2 \rb renew|חַדֵּ֥שׁ\rb* \rb our days|יָמֵ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb as of old|כְּקֶֽדֶם׃\rb*,
\q1 \v 22 \rb unless|כִּ֚י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb You have utterly rejected us|מָאֹ֣ס\rb*\rb |מְאַסְתָּ֔נוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb and remain angry|קָצַ֥פְתָּ\rb* \rb with us|עָלֵ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb beyond measure|עַד־\rb*\rb |מְאֹֽד׃\rb*.
